An awful sequel to one of the best MMOs I've ever played. This game brings shame to the original Ragnarök, which gave many of us MMORPGers our very first taste of what it is to play a MMORPG. Comparisons aside, Ragnarok Online 2 is still a very bad game.
When the game was released in 2013, I've played a few hours and thought that the game itself was kinda generic and a bland MMO but I wanted to give RO2 the benefit of the doubt and I kept playing for something like three months or so (I've probably had around 300 hours of gameplay outside Steam).
As soon as I found that this game was in Steam, I felt like I should came here and make a short review of what RO2 includes. Let's resume it in a few words:
- A horrible pay2win system and a ridiculous amount of grinding to earn enough money to catch up with those who can buy from the cash shop;
- Generic anime graphics;
- A lot of bugs that are never or take a hell of a long amount of time to get fixed;
- Unbalanced classes and a repetitive combat system;
- Generic Quests. A lot of them. Bring X, Kill X monsters, etc.
Just stay away from it. This game is a failure and doesn't worth your time.

Highly recommend this game based on:
* realistic play of man / woman versus elements / hunger / thirst and fatigue;
* Exceptionally beautiful artwork throughout the game, make sure you take time to stop and look at the scenery / lighting;
* A challenging game where I dies I can't recall how many times;
* Exploration of lands where it is easy to get lost, Now I know how someone lost in the woods feels;
* When you do get to survive 5, 10 and 25 days, it is very rewarding;
* Unique Halloween themed '4 Days of Darkness' where you could pick up treats, pumpkin pies and jack-o-laterns;
* A thoroughly well designed game with the thrill for the end user in mind, thanks Hinterland!

