I do really believe Metin2 will come to an end pretty fast here on Steam, and they [developers and managers] really should listen to us [the community] every once in a while...
- The game is indeed outdated, so won't attract much attention. There's this massive grinding, which I love about MMORPG, but most people doesn't, that's why it's the "old school" format of MMORPG;
- Steam's fresh starters can't play with the community because everyone will be way ahead of them. I'm at level 80/120 and I play since 2012 on this account;
- Players will be unable to multi client, while this is possible (and necessary) to do so using the non Steam client. This step is very important. If you're new to Metin2 and want to reach middle/end game DON'T EVEN THINK ABOUT IT without having like 3 or 4 accounts logged simultaneously. Trust me and other advanced users!;
- The item shop. On top of it all (like if it wasn't enough) there's this brutal need of the item shop. In Metin2 you need to buy (with real money) your way in to many of the world maps that you will be playing in, and every time you come out you need to buy a new "ticket". This costs like 5€. Plus in-game money can be bought from the item shop as well, so you take your conclusions;
The truth is that I love Metin2 since a very long time ago, but I'm negatively reviewing it myself here on Steam. It is really not worth anyone's time here. Thanks for reading and I hope it helped.

