I get that people are unhappy about DLC, and I was a bit miffed by that too. But I don't think DLC warrants a negative review of the game. So let's get to the actual game;
If you liked Left 4 Dead, and the idea of opposing sides having wildly different gameplay, but each trying to outdo the other, you'll enjoy this. It's easy for a game like this to make one side too powerful, or have some gimmick that everyone exploits to win - but this game doesn't have that. It never feels unfair, no matter which side or character you play - i think that's a hell of an accomplishment. Better yet, every character meshes well with the others; you never feel like there's a "gimp" character that isn't worth playing. The classes stray from the usual tropes of "fighter, rogue, healer, and buffer", which is a relief. Each class is useful, and each one can antagonize the monster in their own way.
Overall i think it's a remarkable game, in that I really can't find another game to compare it to, yet it's extraordinarily fun, balanced, and has a ton of gameplay options that make me think that this is a game that I could genuinely spend 100+ hours on.

